1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ='''''' '''Annan isä oli luultavasti Per Jonsson Kempe (vanhempi)''''''''''''''=
2 CONT 'https://gw.geneanet.org/imelainenh?n=barck&oc=&p=nils+olofsson&type=fiche
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Claimed mother born 1616 Claimed son born 1620, that would make the grandmother 4 years old at that time of her grandsons birth. 
2 CONT
2 CONT All documented children to Peder Jönsson Kempe-Fahnehielm and Brita Göransdr Armsköld (married 1640-12-04) have been born 1642 and thereafter.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Fahnehielm_nr_406
2 CONT
2 CONT Whoever was Nils Olofsson Barck's mother was not from this couple.
2 CONT
2 CONT Peder Jonsson 'the older' Kempe (Per Jonsson i Näs) has been proposed by some. He was the grandfather of Peder Jönsson Kempe -> Fahnehielm. Per Jonsson (Kempe) was a knight (ryttare) at Östgöta ryttare 1552–1559, which indicates h
2 CONC e must likely have been born before 1532. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Nils Olofsson Barck was born ca. 1620 in Sweden and died 1683 in Hvittis (Huittinen) Finland. That would indicate that his mother, Anna Persdotter Kempe, must have been born no later than 1604 and likely not earlier than 1580. Her
2 CONC  father would then have been likely born after 1515, which makes Per Jonsson (Kempe) i Näs a possible candidate as a father.  His son served as a knight (ryttare) for 20 years in Östgöta ryttare before 1627. His son, Peder Jönsson
2 CONC  Kempe, was born 1596 which places Jon Perssons birth ca. 1575, which matches quite well with the assumed sister's birth between 1580-1604. 
2 CONT
2 CONT If Anna Maria was the Kempe, then her father likely has been the older Kempe Peder Jonsson i Näs. Toisaalta Annan Kempe-sukulaisuus perustuu oletukseen, mikä on mainittu hänen poikansa profiilin yleistiedoissa. Mikä on lähde, mikä
2 CONC  osoittaisi hänen olevan Peder Kempen tytär. Fahnehjelm- suvun lähteet eivät mainitse Peterille Anna-tytärtä!
